  "summary_en": "Book-chapter preprint proposing 'dynamic certification', an adaptive, iterative regulatory framework for embodied AI. Approvals begin with narrow uses and contexts and expand as monitoring evidence accumulates. It is illustrated with an urban delivery robot and links sociotechnical requirements, context of use and system testing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Static regulation cannot keep pace with adaptive, opaque embodied AI systems.",
   "Dynamic certification approves narrow uses and contexts, then expands them as safety evidence accumulates.",
   "A layered framework links sociotechnical context, context of use and system-level testing.",
   "Formal models and specifications are living documents, continually refined through testing and monitoring.",
   "An urban delivery robot is used as a worked example."
  ],
